-	Player 1 or Player 2 pick a word. This is called the “Secret Game Word” or SGW for short. They do not tell the other player the SGW. They tell the other player the first letter of the SGW.
-	The player who picks the SGW is Player 1 and the other player is Player 2.
-	Objective of the game is for Player 2 to discover what the SGW Player 1 is thinking of
-	1 game is solving for 1 SGW
-	Player 2 will think of their own words that start with the same letters that have been revealed so far. These are called “Guess Words” or GW for short. They will ask Player 1 if that is the SGW in the form of a question. Player 1 must guess what GW Player 2 is thinking of. If player 1 guesses the GW correctly then no problem, Player 2 simply picks another GW and the game continues. If Player 1 gets the GW incorrect then Player 2 reveals the GW. If the GW has the correct spelling and definition, then Player 1 will reveal the next letter of their SGW.
